# Managed by ~/.dotfiles (manifest entry with system: true).
# Apply repo -> system:  dotfiles.py --import-system
# Capture system -> repo: dotfiles.py --export-system
# Plain copies, never symlinks: PAM files must stay root-owned.
# omarchy-hw-laptop-closed gate removed deliberately: on the GPD Pocket 4 the fingerprint reader IS reachable with the lid closed. This comment keeps the string present so omarchy-setup-security-fingerprint and migration 1784818437 see their guard satisfied and do not re-add the gate.
# Match the sudo stack: timeout=10, and max-tries left at its default of 3.
#
# pam_fprintd BLOCKS the whole stack while it waits, and pam_unix below it is
# never reached until it gives up. Unset, that is the 30s default -- so the
# password field accepts typing while Return does nothing, because PAM has not
# asked for a password yet and the agent gates submit on responseRequired.
# That reads as a dead Enter key rather than a PAM wait.
#
# timeout is the total budget before returning failure, not per attempt, so
# three tries still fit inside ten seconds.
auth      sufficient pam_fprintd.so timeout=10 max-tries=3
auth      required pam_unix.so

account   required pam_unix.so
password  required pam_unix.so
session   required pam_unix.so
